    <activity label="ula-preview-2-2">
      <title> Matrix operations </title>

      <task label="ula-preview-2-2-a">
        <statement>
	  <p> Compute the scalar multiple
	  <me>
	    -3\left[
	    \begin{array}{rrr}
	    3 \amp 1 \amp 0 \\
	    -4 \amp 3 \amp -1 \\
	    \end{array}
	    \right]
	    </me>.
	  </p>
        </statement>
        <response component="rs-preview"/>
        <solution>
	  <p>
	    <m>\left[\begin{array}{rrr}
	    -9 \amp -3 \amp 0 \\
	    12 \amp -9 \amp 3 \\
	    \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </solution>
        <answer>
	  <p>
	    <m>\left[\begin{array}{rrr}
	    -9 \amp -3 \amp 0 \\
	    12 \amp -9 \amp 3 \\
	    \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </answer>
      </task>

      <task label="ula-preview-2-2-b">
        <statement>
	  <p> Find the sum
	  <me>
	    \left[
	    \begin{array}{rr}
	    0 \amp -3 \\
	    1 \amp -2 \\
	    3 \amp 4 \\
	    \end{array}
	    \right]
	    +
	    \left[
	    \begin{array}{rrr}
	    4 \amp -1 \\
	    -2 \amp 2 \\
	    1 \amp 1 \\
	    \end{array}
	    \right]
	    </me>.
	  </p>
        </statement>
        <response component="rs-preview"/>
        <solution>
	  <p>
	    <m>\left[\begin{array}{rr}
	    4 \amp -4 \\
	    -1 \amp 0 \\
	    4 \amp 5 \\
	    \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </solution>
        <answer>
	  <p>
	    <m>\left[\begin{array}{rr}
	    4 \amp -4 \\
	    -1 \amp 0 \\
	    4 \amp 5 \\
	    \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </answer>
      </task>

      <task label="ula-preview-2-2-c">
        <statement>
	  <p> Suppose that <m>A</m> and <m>B</m> are two matrices.
	  What do we need to know about their shapes before we can
	  form the sum <m>A+B</m>? </p>
        </statement>
        <response component="rs-preview"/>
        <solution>
	  <p>
	    The shapes must be the same.
	  </p>
        </solution>
        <answer>
	  <p>
	    The shapes must be the same.
	  </p>
        </answer>
      </task>

      <task label="ula-preview-2-2-d">
        <statement>
	  <p> The matrix <m>I_n</m>, which we call the <em>
	  identity </em> matrix, is the <m>n\times n</m> matrix whose
	  entries are zero except for the diagonal entries, all of which
	  are 1.
          <idx> matrix, identity </idx>
          For instance,
	  <me>
	    I_3 =
	    \left[
	    \begin{array}{rrr}
	    1 \amp 0 \amp 0 \\
	    0 \amp 1 \amp 0 \\
	    0 \amp 0 \amp 1 \\
	    \end{array}
	    \right]
	    </me>.
	    If we can form the sum <m>A+I_n</m>, what must be true about the
	    matrix <m>A</m>?
	  </p>
        </statement>
        <response component="rs-preview"/>
        <solution>
	  <p>
	    The shape of <m>A</m> must be <m>n\times n</m>.
	  </p>
        </solution>
        <answer>
	  <p>
	    The shape of <m>A</m> must be <m>n\times n</m>.
	  </p>
        </answer>
      </task>

      <task label="ula-preview-2-2-e">
        <statement>
	  <p>
	    Find the matrix <m> A - 2I_3</m> where
	    <me>
	      A =
	      \left[
	      \begin{array}{rrr}
	      1 \amp 2 \amp -2 \\
	      2 \amp -3 \amp 3 \\
	      -2 \amp 3 \amp 4 \\
	      \end{array}
	      \right]
	      </me>.
	  </p>
        </statement>
        <response component="rs-preview"/>
        <solution>
	  <p>
	    <m>
	      A-2I_3 = \left[\begin{array}{rrr}
	      -1 \amp 2 \amp -2 \\
	      2 \amp -5 \amp 3 \\
	      -2 \amp 3 \amp 2 \\
	      \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </solution>
        <answer>
	  <p>
	    <m>
	      A-2I_3 = \left[\begin{array}{rrr}
	      -1 \amp 2 \amp -2 \\
	      2 \amp -5 \amp 3 \\
	      -2 \amp 3 \amp 2 \\
	      \end{array}\right]
	    </m>
	  </p>
        </answer>
      </task>

